kb:0499874b-93ac-5c9e-92b4-f4efbc8069fd a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 575" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "To compute dM, a small value (10−5) was added to the diagonal of the covariance matrix as a regularizer to avoid singularity." .

kb:04f905b6-0d35-5940-aa4c-5b8b942ae042 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 550" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Hence, dM is the effective distance between x and the mean of Y, taking into account the variability in Y." .

kb:06587290-79c1-50d0-bca8-ca1a58f84794 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 564" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "dM from a sample point x in manifold X to the reference distribution computed from manifold Y is the distance from x to the centroid of Y (μY), relative to the directional variability in Y (ruler)." .

