    ner:sentenceText "0.05 0.10 0.15 Capacity *** NS P: number of manifolds N*: critical number of neurons a 0.05 0.10 0.15 0.20 Axis alignment ** Naive Trained Naive Trained Naive Trained Naive Trained 0.7 0.8 0.9 Center alignment *** 15 20 Dimension *** 0.9 1.0 1.1 Radius *** Radius Dimension Center alignment Axis alignment Large Small Training High Low Training High Low Training High Low Training e Naive *** *** ** Arg+/ Phe– Phe+/ Arg– Phe+/ Trp– Probability (linearly separable) Number of neurons (subsampling) 0 1 NData 0 Capacity: α = P/N* d Naive Phe+/Arg– Arg+/Phe– Phe+/Trp– Odor Capacity Fig." .

kb:2e1fb168-35cd-5327-afd7-fa6e60ad5f82 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 162" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Such a directional amplification of activity may also contribute to the decrease in axis alignment observed in pDp, which had a negative effect on manifold capacity." .

kb:2edc3974-5b96-54a4-83af-e25f2683d85f a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 126" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "This analytical framework quantifies the untangledness (‘separability’) of manifolds using manifold capacity2,15,38, a metric that assesses how efficiently manifolds are stored in neural state space for retrieval via linear readout." .

kb:3066bd5a-845e-535e-ab6f-21fe4344e208 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 580" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Current clamp recordings from superficial mitral cells (n = 4) showed that the latency between blue light onset and cessation of action potential firing was approximately 10–20 ms." .

kb:314515f4-c03c-5295-bb10-d4e4c0ab3946 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 138" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "For all three classes, manifold capacity was significantly higher in trained than in naive fish (Fig." .

kb:31515df0-cbd6-55be-ae35-4243fdccbe33 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 196" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "The code for manifold capacity analysis is provided as Supplementary Software (zip file)." .

kb:31c26915-71e2-5aa1-b8dd-321cb171cff8 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 492" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "d, Mean cosine distance between activity patterns evoked by different odors (3 trials each) in naïve and trained fish." .

kb:31da19af-ec4a-5c17-9b11-eb458ed9ff64 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 221" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "neurons a 0.05 0.10 0.15 0.20 Axis alignment ** Naive Trained Naive Trained Naive Trained Naive Trained 0.7 0.8 0.9 Center alignment *** 15 20 Dimension *** 0.9 1.0 1.1 Radius *** Radius Dimension Center alignment Axis alignment Large Small Training High Low Training High Low Training High Low Training e Naive *** *** ** Arg+/ Phe– Phe+/ Arg– Phe+/ Trp– Probability (linearly separable) Number of neurons (subsampling) 0 1 NData 0 Capacity: α = P/N* d Naive Phe+/Arg– Arg+/Phe– Phe+/Trp– Odor Capacity Fig." .

kb:322569d4-0bfd-5a3e-bf29-b007de4aab86 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 261" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "These results show that many neurons exhibit a classical off-response at the end of stimulation." .

kb:329fd566-e9ce-5656-a255-49667cead109 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 147" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "d, Manifold capacity as a function of time in different training groups (mean ± s.d.; 3-s time window, centered on the specified time points)." .

kb:338436be-037c-5a6d-b7d1-5c3347bce765 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 315" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Consistent with previous observations39,40,54–56, trial-to-trial variability in pDp was substantially higher than in the olfactory bulb (Extended Data Fig." .

kb:33d15ea7-34ef-5fb8-92c1-f41e4331e2ae a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 21" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Stimuli may thus be classified by a systematic organization of neural manifolds according to semantic categories, independent of whether or not manifolds are attractor states." .

kb:35bb2c49-5fb6-5117-9313-1d74018bbb48 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 81" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "These observations gave rise to the hypothesis that learning results in the formation of neuronal assemblies that represent odor objects and mediate pattern classification by convergent dynamics20; however, recent analyses of neuronal activity in piriform cortex did not reveal obvious signatures of attractor states." .

kb:366cc4e7-f209-5323-a4f7-cee453d466e4 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 304" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Hence, measures of separability based on geometrical features of representational manifolds predicted olfactory discrimination behavior in juvenile fish, indicating that geometrical modifications of representational manifolds contributed to learned changes in behavior." .

kb:3672c872-ea28-59aa-bb87-932cf43d7bf5 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 302" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "9d), as observed in juvenile fish (Fig." .

kb:3778046a-9a12-5eef-9df1-4b4bb283935e a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 384" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Naive Trained Naive Trained 0.7 0.8 0.9 Center alignment *** 15 20 Dimension *** 0.9 1.0 1.1 Radius *** Radius Dimension Center alignment Axis alignment Large Small Training High Low Training High Low Training High Low Training e Naive *** *** ** Arg+/ Phe– Phe+/ Arg– Phe+/ Trp– Probability (linearly separable) Number of neurons (subsampling) 0 1 NData 0 Capacity: α = P/N* d Naive Phe+/Arg– Arg+/Phe– Phe+/Trp– Odor Capacity Fig." .

kb:38ba83e7-5415-5da4-a7ec-fc769abc7d92 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 125" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Manifold capacity analysis can therefore be used to determine how learning modifies geometrical features of representational manifolds, and how these modifications collectively affect the classification of activity representing learned and novel inputs." .

kb:39868fec-b805-519c-b3f9-9b986de0624e a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 108" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Hence, training (passive odor exposure or active learning) enhanced odor classification in pDp without establishing obvious attractor dynamics." .

kb:3a46dd25-7b46-52f7-9665-65b57bfd61ab a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 22" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "The notion that neural manifolds organize relevant information in neuronal state space implies that geometrical and statistical properties of manifolds are relevant for neural computation2." .

