kb:e467951a-434e-5386-9feb-c44d0ffe90f5 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 226" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Before forming a seal, neurons were approached within the tissue using low pressure (20 mbar)." .

kb:e4ef05d4-5eee-5090-8f96-644e4a8cc572 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 278" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Behavioral odor discrimination training had only minor effects on the mean amplitude and variability of odor responses in pDp." .

kb:e4f4ac54-678d-5375-aaa4-cb0aeaf3fe62 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 23" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Nature Neuroscience Article https://doi.org/10.1038/s41593-026-02429-3 Representational manifolds and olfactory memory Our findings indicate that pDp contains a continuous representation of odor space that is modified, but not discretized, by constraining activity onto neural manifolds." .

kb:e58fe405-93ba-50f3-962a-3bf4e03831ca a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 586" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Nieh, E." .

kb:e5a42680-7601-524e-8115-01aa5d031d60 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 244" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Neurons from fish in the same condition were pooled." .

kb:e5df3adc-4ae6-5de3-9259-e16151ebd794 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 256" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Furthermore, we sorted neurons by k-means clustering into four clusters based on their firing rate time courses, independently for each odor (b,c)." .

kb:e690a413-277f-5395-96c0-ec508adf1f53 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 422" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "tance (odor–odor) NS *** *** Trained (Arg+/Phe–) AA BA 0 0.2 0.4 0.6 NS NS Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA AA BA –5 5 –5 5 UMAP 1 UMAP 1 –4 4 UMAP 2 –4 4 UMAP 2 Arg Phe Trp GCA TCA TDCA Trained (Arg+/Phe–) Cosine distance Naive Trained 200 400 600 Number of neurons 0.6 0.7 0.8 0.9 LDA Cross-validation accuracy *** *** * *** *** ** *** *** ** *** *** ** *** *** ** *** *** * Naive Phe+/Arg– Arg+/Phe– Phe+/Trp– Naive Naive Fig." .

kb:e74223f6-1cf2-5a33-b7f3-4ebbe29fad90 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 608" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Effective radius measures how far the points spread away from the manifold center, and is normalized by the length of the manifold center." .

kb:e7437390-dc71-54bc-baad-00e03fbe52c4 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 468" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "ζ scores are combined and normalized measures similar to z-scores that quantify appetitive behavior in response to each odor." .

kb:e7965cd4-f24b-579e-8deb-6292bced9dbd a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 153" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Consistent with these findings, manifold capacity in adult pDp was significantly higher in trained than in naive fish (Extended Data Fig." .

kb:e7cf3f81-8fbd-587d-a403-e98ae890d24e a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 532" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Standard GLUE theory expresses manifold capacity as a function of four parameters that measure interpretable geometrical features of manifolds and their correlations37: (1) effective manifold AA AA AA BA BA BA 0 5 10 15 dE ** *** NS AA→AA AA→BA BA→AA BA→BA 0 2.5 5.0 7.5 dM 0 2 4 6 8 10 –95 0 95 2 4 6 −1.9 0 1.9 a c e b d f ∆dE dE dM ∆dM Trained - Naive Naive Trained - Naive Naive Naive Naive Trained (Arg+/Phe–) Trained (Arg+/Phe–) Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA AA BA CS+ CS– AA3 TDCA TCA GCA Reference Sample Reference Sample Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA AA BA *** * NS NS CS+ CS– AA3 TDCA TCA GCA ×102 ×10 2 Trained Trained Fi" .

kb:e7ea4848-6202-56d9-8e49-dee7e4eadf71 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 305" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Juvenile fish were kept in 1.1-l tanks (Tecniplast ZB11TK)." .

kb:e89fab0b-1691-56d0-bd4e-44e6bfa564bc a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 435" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "y as a function of four parameters that measure interpretable geometrical features of manifolds and their correlations37: (1) effective manifold AA AA AA BA BA BA 0 5 10 15 dE ** *** NS AA→AA AA→BA BA→AA BA→BA 0 2.5 5.0 7.5 dM 0 2 4 6 8 10 –95 0 95 2 4 6 −1.9 0 1.9 a c e b d f ∆dE dE dM ∆dM Trained - Naive Naive Trained - Naive Naive Naive Naive Trained (Arg+/Phe–) Trained (Arg+/Phe–) Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA AA BA CS+ CS– AA3 TDCA TCA GCA Reference Sample Reference Sample Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA AA BA *** * NS NS CS+ CS– AA3 TDCA TCA GCA ×102 ×10 2 Trained Trained Fig." .

kb:ea2b9b82-765b-5f06-bc86-93c9abc764d2 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 11" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Hence, neural manifolds may support classification and learning by organizing representations according to semantic variables and facilitating access to relevant information." .

kb:ea6d66dd-018c-5127-9576-70ca23b195e1 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 258" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Furthermore, we defined a persistence index to identify neurons with elevated activity that extended beyond stimulus offset (f)." .

kb:ead02242-b3c2-53c1-8299-eebf291f09f2 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 18" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Yellow and purple ellipsoids depict neural manifolds (sets of activity vectors evoked by an odor, pooled over trials and time points)." .

kb:eb6c1431-03df-5a11-ac67-a2a66637b618 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 113" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Attractor dynamics in networks with learning rules inferred from in vivo data." .

kb:eb9653af-bd91-5efb-9c95-a91c18b0db71 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 229" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "ROIs were aligned between trials with fast Fourier transform cross-correlation and individual neurons were manually redrawn or deleted depending on the quality of trial-by-trial alignment." .

kb:ec0172c5-cee2-5d48-83ae-e6f04127269d a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 398" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "vidual training day −1 0 1 Appetitive score ζ 0 2 4 6 8 10 Mean firing rate (Hz) Density 0 2 4 6 8 10 Time (s) Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA Odor Trained Odor 0 2 4 6 8 10 Time (s) 0.5 1.0 1.5 2.0 Firing rate (Hz) 0.5 1.0 1.5 2.0 Firing rate (Hz) Naive 0 1 2 3 Mean firing rate (Hz) *** *** *** Individual training ~4 days Acclimate 3 days Group training 11 days Naive Phe+/ Arg– Arg+/ Phe– Phe+/ Trp– CS+ – Arg Phe CS– – Phe Arg Trp Phe Training group Naive (n = 6) Arg+/Phe– (n = 9) Phe+/Trp– (n = 6) Phe+/Arg– (n = 10) 10 –0 10 –1 10 –2 10 –3 10 –4 Naive Phe+/Arg– Arg+/Phe– Phe+/Trp– Fig." .

kb:ec07f36d-74f9-5b77-817c-80c0a42679f5 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 273" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Percentage of neurons showing persistent responses to one or multiple odors, separated by training groups." .

kb:ec0a3cd9-228c-5df4-8818-e7ba9250acad a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 569" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Note that dM increased selectively in the direction from learned to other odors (dMA1→other; dMA2→other), and this effect generalized to the related odor (dMA3→other)." .

kb:ec404598-f5da-59c0-9523-a75c8ce3b978 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 32" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "c, Training enhanced the separation of neural manifolds representing conditioned odors (CS+, CS−) from representations of other odors." .

