    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "As manifolds typically have different shapes, dM in the direction from manifold A to manifold B (dMA→B) is usually different from dM in the opposite direction (dMB→A), providing information about manifold geometry (Fig." .

