kb:f0c65c91-d57d-5f1b-872c-4579bbc37161 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 574" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "dM with X as sample and Y as reference was defined as: dM (X, Y) = 1 |X| ∑ x∈X √(x −μY) TS−1 Y (x −μY), where |X| is the number of points in the manifold X, x is a point in the manifold X, μY is the center of the manifold Y, and SY is the covariance matrix of the manifold Y." .

