    ner:sentenceText "Standard GLUE theory expresses manifold capacity as a function of four parameters that measure interpretable geometrical features of manifolds and their correlations37: (1) effective manifold AA AA AA BA BA BA 0 5 10 15 dE ** *** NS AA→AA AA→BA BA→AA BA→BA 0 2.5 5.0 7.5 dM 0 2 4 6 8 10 –95 0 95 2 4 6 −1.9 0 1.9 a c e b d f ∆dE dE dM ∆dM Trained - Naive Naive Trained - Naive Naive Naive Naive Trained (Arg+/Phe–) Trained (Arg+/Phe–) Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA AA BA CS+ CS– AA3 TDCA TCA GCA Reference Sample Reference Sample Phe Arg Trp TDCA TCA GCA AA BA *** * NS NS CS+ CS– AA3 TDCA TCA GCA ×102 ×10 2 Trained Trained Fig." .

kb:ade59b5c-293c-5f28-b403-7af31a1bdcc8 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 332" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "Optogenetic silencing of the olfactory bulb within 10 – 20 ms was achieved using Tg[dlx4/6:Chr2YFP] fish, which express channelrhodopsin-2 fused to YFP in superficial inhibitory interneurons of the olfactory bulb63,64 (f)." .

