    rdfs:label "sentence 16" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "We first used two distance measures, Euclidean distance (dE) and Mahalanobis distance (dM), to characterize basic geometrical relationships between neural manifolds in activity space (the state space where each dimension represents activity of one neuron)." .

kb:b599d72c-d5db-5ad1-a5d2-88c158d168a8 a ner:Sentence ;
    rdfs:label "sentence 473" ;
    ner:partOfDocumentVersion kb:a6a2cf3f-c89a-56c0-88fa-031f7afd0daa ;
    ner:sentenceText "dE was increased between the CS+, the CS− and the third amino acid (AA3), and between amino acids and bile acids, whereas dE between bile acids was not significantly different." .

